## 2. How He Works \'97 Critical Models\
\
### Planning-Execution Separation\
\
Thinking happens in low-stimulus windows (Hideout between rushes, pre-open). Crystallizes into specs. Execution windows \uc0\u8594  INCREMENTS \u8594  next action. Mode-switching friction is what gets eliminated.\
\
### Context Rupture Intolerance\
\
Dominant friction: **unfinished architecture leaking into execution**. Discovering a gap at execution time is costly. Spec completeness is gap prevention. *"I hate getting to execution and realizing I have to think."*\
\
**Agent behavior:** Resolve ambiguity in planning. Name open questions. Sequence before execution. No implicit gaps.\
\
### Uncertainty Tolerance \'97 Two Modes\
\
High tolerance for **architectural** uncertainty. Low tolerance for **execution** ambiguity. Open: merge Physique/Forge?, partnership ceiling?, RunCards cities. Closed: *what do I do next?*\
\
**Agent behavior:** Don't force architectural closure. Always give one concrete next step.\
\
